# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/fusion-2 window (the prefill levers on the ship stack: the prefill SDPA with one q chunk per core, WPP, and the 13x10 matmul grids, M1; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fusion-2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-6 is the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (the oneq lever needs its binary; every arm without the flag runs that binary with the lever off). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# X0: the card state before the window: status, a rescan of the topology, an all-four reset. READ: four cards present and healthy, the fabric as measured, the compute grid
# of the run (AVAILABLE WORKER CORE COUNT; 13x10 since the firmware unlock: both prefill levers read it from the device and keep the served ops on anything narrower, with a
# fell-back line that fails the smoke on purpose), no other window driver alive. Stop rule: anything else. (The owner stops the node agent and unserves production before
# it, and restores production after Z, with the cutover pack's own steps.) Duration (estimate): 20 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status rescan reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-6
